{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/782766-changeling-hunters","id":782766,"title":"Changeling Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T06:38:44-08:00","id":782766,"title":"Changeling Hunters","content":"I notice that there are no conspiracies dedicated to hunting Changelings. They are sufficiently weird and different enough that they should warrant a Changeling specific Conspiracy. I imagine a group of Druids who worship the Tuatha De Dannan and believe the Changelings are the True Fairies' rightful property, and at the behest of their gods will track down Changelings to return them to their masters. Their Endowment should be The Wyrd, a form a Druid magic that can do things like block a Changeling's access to the Hedge or render null and void a specific Contract a Changeling has if the Druid is aware of it. They would also have access to Changeling Lore that would allow them to develop tactics that are geared towards catching The Lost.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that Tier 1 hunters would go after a Changeling if, say for example, they didn't know what a Fetch was or that their family member or spouse was a Fetch this whole time, and they happen to walk in on a Changeling killing its Fetch. Imagine the horror of seeing your loved one turning into a pile of stones a twigs after being stabbed in the chest. This sort of Tier 1 introduction to the Vigil could serve as a gateway for a Teir 2 Compact consisting of people who have lost loved ones to Changelings, not knowing that their loved one was a Fetch. A support group of sorts that looks for people who have suffered this specific loss and tries to hunt down the Changeling that did it.<br /> <br /> What kind of Compacts, and Conspiracies (if you have a different idea than mine), and new Endowments would you make for Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T06:48:33-08:00","id":782774,"title":"","content":"That doesn't sound like a Hunter organization, it sounds like a cult. Its a cool idea overall it's just &quot;worship gods and serve them by returning their runaway slaves&quot; doesn't seem like a ... Vigil situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T07:15:17-08:00","id":782780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/782766-changeling-hunters?p=782774#post782774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't sound like a Hunter organization, it sounds like a cult. Its a cool idea overall it's just &quot;worship gods and serve them by returning their runaway slaves&quot; doesn't seem like a ... Vigil situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like we haven't seen that situation before. Knights of Saint George? Cainite Heresy? Cheiron? So on and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T07:18:42-08:00","id":782783,"title":"","content":"You've got a point. Though it is difficult for me to think of a conspiracy of Changeling hunters from another angle though. I was going for something that was related to the Fae religiously, like how the Caininite Heresy and the Knights of St. George are both religiously motivated, focused on one particular group of supernaturals, and have a group of Endowments that are geared towards that specific type of supernatural monster alone. While yet another group of Christian hunters seems a little off for this one, I figured a group of modern Druids would be more appropriate since the Fae are a cannon part of the Druid religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:17:11-08:00","id":782853,"title":"","content":"There is a fan made group called the Regency of Thorns which sees Changelings as invaders from alien reality sent by Arcadian Gods. Glaumorweaver has also suggested a group which hunts Changeling for magical luck, if I'm not mistaken, and personally i also have an idea for a group of assassins bound by ancient Pact to hunt down Changelings is exchange for their ability to create Fetch like doubles. Anyway, the idea of order of Druids who sees the True Fae as Tuatha incarnated does seems appropriate and interesting.<br /> <br /> EDIT- also, I wrote this thing- the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/405575-new-conspiracy-orchestra-fatalibus\">Orchestra Fatalibus</a>, founded during the French Revolution which still fights against those who bind humanity's freedom and silence their voice from the great choir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-09-2015, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:26:17-08:00","id":782857,"title":"","content":"Revlid also created a Conspiracy called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/344770-repost-revild-s-hotel-mascaron\">Hotel Mascaron</a>, with some 2e conversion notes written by Amechra <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358705-gmc-hotel-mascarone-some-tweaks\">here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:49:25-08:00","id":782876,"title":"","content":"Have a look at Dream Catchers - a full sized fae fan-supplement. Link in my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:27:44-08:00","id":783001,"title":"","content":"These are some interesting ideas for Changeling Hunters.<br /> <br /> I wonder, what sort of home brew endowments have you thought of for the general purpose Conspiracies to deal with Changelings? I know, for example, that the Catholic church views Fae as angels who were cast from Heaven to Earth for being mischievous (as opposed to demons who were cast into Hell for being evil), so Malleus Maleficarum might have a Benediction or two that are flavored with that belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:59:11-08:00","id":783019,"title":"","content":"Task Force: Valkyrie Advanced Armory coil/rail-gun that fires a sliver of cold iron? A bit elaborate against most targets when a standard firearm would work just as well (if not better), but singularly devastating against targets weak to the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T01:38:19-08:00","id":785820,"title":"","content":"One of the first endowments any Changeling hunter would need is something to actually see through the Mask otherwise it will be incredibly hard to even find them. Mind you, at the same time it should not be too easy either, since the strength of the Mask is one of the strong points of Changelings.<br /> <br /> Note that in mythology changelings are scared by the sound of church bells, seems like a good basis for another endowment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T11:00:27-08:00","id":786080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/782766-changeling-hunters?p=785820#post785820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the first endowments any Changeling hunter would need is something to actually see through the Mask otherwise it will be incredibly hard to even find them. Mind you, at the same time it should not be too easy either, since the strength of the Mask is one of the strong points of Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div> The other possiblity is to make the Changeling really hard to find, but easy to defeat once you find them.<br /> <br /> The good thing is that with so many different groups there's room for both ways. Some Hunters groups should have a way of seeing through the Mask, not all of them need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:50:16-08:00","id":786968,"title":"","content":"I always thought you had to be really cold-blooded to be dedicated to hunting changelings. Provided you knew what they were, at least.<br /> <br /> The others I could easily understand, but changelings always seemed the cowering victims of the World of Darkness. I appreciate they can be monsters as easy as everyone else but they're about the only template I thought hunter books were justified in for the most part leaving alone in Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> Maybe some sort of 'Truther' organization that believes the numbers of missing persons in the world are inflated by shills paid by the government who create fake lives and leave them? It might not fit depending on how common fetches are. Perhaps they think fetches are some sort of undercover agents sent by the government to spy on the populace?<br /> <br /> What about a group that is aware of the magical power of changeling contracts, and hunts them in order to empower or enrich themselves?<br /> <br /> In my changeling game there was a group called the Order of Prometheus, which was tremendously misleading to those well aware of the various gamelines. But they had seemed to make a deal with a True Fae who wanted the others destroyed and, in turn, were working to militarize the Hedge, having captured changelings and forced them into pacts to keep portals open. It was seriously risky business practically destined to blow up in horrific fashion but the concept of people who weren't fully aware of the danger trying to take advantage of it for nationalistic or monetary purposes rang true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-15-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T14:58:30-08:00","id":786977,"title":"","content":"The cycle of abuse. Changelings are victims, but if your psychosis includes turning everyone who strikes a match while wearing red into a pillar of fire; going through a durance does not give you a licence to commit murder.<br /> <br /> Good hunters won't jump straight to murder as the first and only solution for changings who can legitimately make the insanity defence (that's most of them). It's one of the reasons the Conspiracy in Dream Catchers are diplomats and lawyers who're qualified to solve problems with a pledge rather than a gun, but a Changeling who's causing harm through their insanity or their immorality is still causing harm and something must be done. Violently or otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:40:41-08:00","id":787127,"title":"","content":"Hunter class 306 - Changelings: Counseling or Kerosene?<br /> <br /> It would depend on how much of a nuisance the local courts and motleys are making of themselves. An Autumn court gone too far (both in the fear spreading/harvesting sense, and in the losing subtly sense), could easily make themselves a target of local hunter groups. The relative difficulty of detecting Changelings (due to the Mask), and their extremely varied nature likely limit the organizational response the Conspiracies would have (though I can see Pledge-burned Loyalists of Thule and thrill seeking Ashwood Abbey as having the most contact and institutional view points).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T17:15:01-08:00","id":787722,"title":"","content":"There's a fan-splat for Hunter, Skin and Bones, that features a hostile-to-changelings dedicated compact/conspiracy. It's made up of Fetches and people who believe that the Fetches are the real people, with some added lies spun by a True Fae patron.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is that because this, to me, is the most likely origin for a changeling-dedicated compact or conspiracy, especially one of a hostile slant.<br /> <br /> The big problem with hunting changelings is that they have the strongest masquerade of any of the existent supernaturals. Even demons are more inherently visible than changelings are, courtesy of glitches. Once you find them, you then have to come up with a justification for hunting them; it's not impossible, as the previous posters have pointed out, but at the same time, changelings are kind of the underdog of the World of Darkness. Unless you've seen them go insane, or been on the receiving end of the bad ones' depredations, generally you're going to go after them because of pure xenophobia.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why most of the compacts and conspiracies in Dream Catchers tend to have a generic anti-fae approach, or even are more inclined towards the True Fae first, unless they're misled about the actual relationship between changelings and true fae, or prejudiced by the presence of fetches in their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}